# Production env for the dashboard bundle (`vite build`).
#
# Vite reads env files from the **dashboard's own directory**, not the repo root —
# `vite.config.mts` calls `loadEnv(mode, process.cwd(), "")`, and the build runs
# with `yarn --cwd mosaic-dashboard`. So the root `.env.production` configures the
# *editor* only; anything the dashboard bundle needs has to live here.
#
# This file is committed and holds no secrets. Every `VITE_`-prefixed value is
# inlined into the public JavaScript bundle, so anything sensitive must be a
# server-side variable on Vercel instead (DATABASE_URL, COOKIE_SECRET) and must
# never be named with the VITE_ prefix.

# Storage backend: presence of this variable selects the Neon API over IndexedDB
# (see `src/lib/storage/index.ts`).
#
# Empty is meaningful and correct here. The serverless functions are deployed
# alongside the dashboard, so the API is same-origin and the request paths are
# already root-relative (`/api/boards`, `/api/health`). `api.ts` builds URLs as
# `${baseUrl}/api/...`, which with an empty baseUrl produces exactly that.
#
# Do not delete this line and do not comment it out: an *absent* variable means
# IndexedDB, which would leave production storing every board in one visitor's
# browser instead of in Postgres.
VITE_API_URL=

# Where the editor is mounted. Defaults to "/app/" in BoardPage.tsx, which matches
# the nginx layout in Dockerfile / docker/nginx.conf, so it is spelled out here to
# make the coupling to that nginx config obvious rather than implicit. `vercel.json`
# rewrites `/app` to the editor bundle in dist/editor, and nginx does the same job
# for the Docker deployment.
VITE_EDITOR_BASE=/app/

# Public base path. "/" because the dashboard is the site root in both deployments:
# Vercel (rewrites "/" to dist/index.html) and nginx (dashboard at /, editor at
# /app/). Kept explicit because the router's route table is written assuming the
# app is mounted at the root — see the note in `.env.development`.
MOSAIC_DASHBOARD_BASE=/